    "substitutions": "BoE Millennium public download is 1086-2016 (v3.1, last modified 2024-09-26, max year 2016); paper's authors updated to 2022 internally. 2017-2022 levels not in public BoE file \u2013 spliced using ONS public generators: ABMI (chained-volume GDP, PN2), D7BT (CPI 2015=100, MM23), UKPOP (mid-year UK population), and World Bank WDI FM.LBL.BMNY.CN broad money for M4/M0 growth (Bank Rate 2017-2022 hand-collected annual averages from BoE official history 0.29/0.60/0.75/0.22/0.10/1.27). England GDP per capita, CPI and money 2017-2022 grown at UK GDP per capita (ABMI/UKPOP), CPI D7BT, and WB broad money growth, anchored to 2016 Millennium levels \u2013 growth approximation preserves paper's per-capita growth definition. M0 2017-2022 uses same WB broad-money growth as proxy because narrow-monetary-base public annual series 2017-2022 not retrievable via automatable BoE database (JS-only interface, FRED M0 series timeout) \u2013 documented as proxy. VAR estimation uses OLS VAR(2) per century subperiod to proxy TVP-VAR-SV (random-walk \u03a6, A, SV with fat tails estimated via Gibbs in paper); identification via Cholesky y-first equals max-FEV horizon-1 (Angeletos et al. 2020 proof). Four-variable sign restrictions approximated by 5000 random orthonormal Q draws filtering AD: y+p+m+rate+ vs MS: y+p+m+rate- on impact; natural-rate r-star proxied by 5-year centred MA of ex-post real Bank Rate (Bank Rate minus CPI inflation) vs paper's DFM Lubik-Matthes 5-year-ahead forecast and Schmelzing real rate \u2013 difference 3-4pp noted."
